<parameter name="summary">Patient meets most criteria for CPAP coverage, including age 52, documented in-person pre-test evaluation, treatment by the treating practitioner, and severity tier A with AHI of 22 events/hour. However, the sleep test fails criterion I3 because it is a Type IV home sleep test with only 2 channels, whereas policy requires Type IV tests to measure at least 3 channels. Refer to nurse for review of the test adequacy.""}

